WEBVTT

00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:43.835
"Europe, 1943 "

00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:07.336
Wh-What is that?

00:02:44.456 --> 00:02:50.170
Since ancient times, humankind has
continually battled with the abnormal.

00:02:50.379 --> 00:02:56.218
And always at the forefront
of these battles were the "Witches,"

00:02:56.426 --> 00:02:58.970
teenage girls wielding the power of magic.

00:03:04.768 --> 00:03:07.854
But, in the year 1939,

00:03:08.063 --> 00:03:13.735
Europe was suddenly besieged
by a wholly overwhelming foe.

00:03:15.821 --> 00:03:19.658
Humankind named them "Neurois."

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:25.247
No one knew from where
the Neurois came or why,

00:03:25.455 --> 00:03:28.375
but it was a fact that their attacks

00:03:28.583 --> 00:03:32.295
drove people from their
home cities and countries.

00:03:36.591 --> 00:03:42.639
In an effort to counter the Neurois,
humankind developed "Striker Units,"

00:03:42.848 --> 00:03:47.018
a new breed of magic brooms
to amplify Witches' magic power

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:50.063
and allow them to take flight.

00:03:52.941 --> 00:03:58.155
Powerful Witches from around
the world were then dispatched

00:03:58.363 --> 00:04:02.617
to the front lines in Europe.

00:05:07.891 --> 00:05:12.562
"Strike Witches Movie"

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:23.073
"August 2nd, 1945"
"Belgica airspace"

00:05:39.798 --> 00:05:43.927
"Karlsland Air Force
1st Independent Special Operations Wing"

00:05:43.927 --> 00:05:47.514
"Major Heidemarie W. Schnaufer"

00:05:50.225 --> 00:05:52.936
All clear today.

00:05:53.144 --> 00:05:55.730
My shift is almost over.

00:05:57.649 --> 00:05:59.860
The moon is so beautiful!

00:06:00.068 --> 00:06:02.612
Maybe I'll keep flying a bit longer.

00:06:07.409 --> 00:06:08.785
<i>This is St. Trend base.</i>

00:06:08.994 --> 00:06:11.997
Major Heidemarie. What is your status?

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:15.709
R-Right. This is Heidemarie.

00:06:15.917 --> 00:06:19.170
Umm... Nothing out of the ordinary here.

00:06:19.379 --> 00:06:20.171
Understood.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:24.593
The Neurois in Karlsland seem
to have stopped for the past half-month.

00:06:24.801 --> 00:06:29.097
Yes. I just hope things remain quiet.

00:06:29.306 --> 00:06:30.223
Ag reed.

00:06:30.432 --> 00:06:31.558
But be careful.

00:06:31.766 --> 00:06:35.478
We're still not fully familiar
with Neuroi behavior--

00:06:37.606 --> 00:06:38.773
Huh?

00:06:38.982 --> 00:06:41.651
St. Trond? Please respond.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.194
St.--

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:44.905
A Neuroi?!

00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:49.034
Alert! Neuroi detected!

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:50.660
It's located...

00:06:50.869 --> 00:06:52.370
...below?!

00:07:00.462 --> 00:07:03.840
It was so close, yet I didn't even notice it?

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.724
Target... acquired.

00:07:15.769 --> 00:07:17.270
It transformed!

00:07:19.022 --> 00:07:21.775
It went into the clouds! It's noticed me!

00:07:23.693 --> 00:07:25.195
Behind...?!

00:07:32.744 --> 00:07:34.245
It's fast!

00:07:45.131 --> 00:07:46.257
You're good.

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:47.968
But...

00:08:10.323 --> 00:08:11.950
This is the end.

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:29.592
<i>This is St. Trend base'.!</i>

00:08:29.801 --> 00:08:31.761
Major Heidemarie! What's happened?!

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:33.722
U-Umm...

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:35.682
A Neuroi appeared.

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:37.851
A Neuroi?! Are you fighting it now?!

00:08:38.059 --> 00:08:41.938
Oh, no. I already destroyed it.

00:08:43.356 --> 00:08:45.900
I'd like to hear the details.
Return to base quickly!

00:08:46.109 --> 00:08:49.112
Understood, Lieutenant Colonel Mina.

00:08:56.411 --> 00:09:01.249
"Yokosuka, Fuso Empire"

00:09:13.428 --> 00:09:16.097
Yoshika!

00:09:16.306 --> 00:09:18.516
Where did you 9Q?!

00:09:22.395 --> 00:09:24.564
Yoshika!

00:09:34.699 --> 00:09:36.201
Michiko!

00:09:36.201 --> 00:09:40.413
"Miyafuji Yoshika
Former Fuso Imperial Navy Sergeant"

00:09:40.955 --> 00:09:42.874
Come, come, come!

00:09:43.958 --> 00:09:45.460
Huh?

00:09:52.133 --> 00:09:57.263
Isn't this the same bear cub
you helped this past spring?

00:09:57.472 --> 00:10:00.016
Yeah. He's sure grown a lot, huh?

00:10:00.225 --> 00:10:02.268
Y-Yeah.

00:10:03.561 --> 00:10:06.397
Yoshika. How is your studying going?

00:10:06.606 --> 00:10:09.734
You're applying to
Teito Girls' Medical School, right?

00:10:11.486 --> 00:10:14.364
Actually, it hasn't been going well...

00:10:14.572 --> 00:10:17.033
It's understandable. You were
busy fighting the Neurois.

00:10:17.242 --> 00:10:18.576
Yeah...

00:10:18.785 --> 00:10:22.997
But I need to catch up
before next year's entrance exam.

00:10:23.206 --> 00:10:26.584
<i>I am</i> going to be a great doctor!

00:10:30.088 --> 00:10:32.465
That must be his mom!

00:10:32.674 --> 00:10:35.301
Thanks! You can let us off here!

00:10:40.265 --> 00:10:41.933
Bye-bye!

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:45.645
Oh, right! The herbs!

00:10:45.854 --> 00:10:48.273
I found some Saint John's wort!

00:10:48.481 --> 00:10:51.776
Really?! That works great on cuts and bruises!

00:10:51.985 --> 00:10:53.486
Where'd you find it?!

00:11:02.412 --> 00:11:03.913
Oh, no!

00:11:05.123 --> 00:11:06.791
Be careful, Yoshika!

00:11:13.131 --> 00:11:14.632
Come here!

00:11:17.385 --> 00:11:19.846
Okay! You're safe now!

00:11:20.889 --> 00:11:22.515
Thank goodness...

00:11:27.437 --> 00:11:29.230
Yoshika!

00:11:29.439 --> 00:11:30.940
Sorry!

00:11:31.941 --> 00:11:33.735
Hang on tight!

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:37.071
Yoshika!

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:46.831
Yoshika!

00:11:56.799 --> 00:11:58.301
Yoshika!

00:11:59.719 --> 00:12:01.221
Yoshika!

00:12:02.388 --> 00:12:04.515
Wow, that scared me!

00:12:14.651 --> 00:12:16.152
A Witch?

00:12:18.696 --> 00:12:19.614
I'm flying...

00:12:19.822 --> 00:12:22.200
Rescuing the dog was important,

00:12:22.408 --> 00:12:25.745
but you should've considered
your own swimming aptitude.

00:12:25.954 --> 00:12:28.248
L-I'm sorry...

00:12:28.456 --> 00:12:30.208
Just as long as you understand.

00:12:31.584 --> 00:12:33.461
Thank you!

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:38.883
I'm glad we're safe and sound!

00:12:39.092 --> 00:12:41.135
I'm so glad, Yoshika!

00:12:41.344 --> 00:12:42.303
Michiko!

00:12:42.512 --> 00:12:43.680
Yoshikam?

00:12:43.888 --> 00:12:47.141
Umm, would you happen to
be Ensign Miyafuji Yoshika?!

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:49.769
Huh? How do you know my name?

00:12:49.978 --> 00:12:52.021
M-My al°0logiesl

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:57.610
I'm Hattori Shizuka, a first-year student
at the Fuso Imperial Naval Academy!

00:12:57.819 --> 00:13:01.906
L-I've always looked up to you,
Ensign Miyafuji!

00:13:02.115 --> 00:13:05.576
You saved the Akagi aircraft carrier
on your very first flight,

00:13:05.785 --> 00:13:07.996
and you fought right alongside
the super-aces of the 501st

00:13:08.204 --> 00:13:10.790
to save not just Gallia, but even Venezia!

00:13:10.999 --> 00:13:12.625
You're amazingly amazing!

00:13:12.834 --> 00:13:14.252
Oh.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:20.633
Major Sakamoto has told me about
your many heroic deeds in Europe!

00:13:20.842 --> 00:13:22.593
Huh? Ms. Sakamoto?

00:13:22.802 --> 00:13:26.723
Yes! In fact, I've come today to
bring you orders from Major Sakamoto

00:13:26.931 --> 00:13:29.642
to study abroad in Europe!

00:13:29.851 --> 00:13:30.893
Eurgpe?

00:13:31.102 --> 00:13:32.603
Study abroad?

00:13:38.651 --> 00:13:42.280
"Miyafuji Medical Clinic"

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:46.534
"You Can Do It!"
"Teito Girls' Medical School"

00:13:48.077 --> 00:13:51.039
I didn't know you were an ensign, Yoshika!

00:13:51.247 --> 00:13:55.043
Yeah! It was my reward for liberating Romagna!

00:13:55.251 --> 00:13:57.462
<i>R-Reward?</i>

00:13:59.255 --> 00:14:00.631
Oh, really?

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:04.052
Yoshika, studying abroad
at a European medical school...

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:09.682
Yes! In fact, I've been asked to
accompany her as her attendant!

00:14:09.891 --> 00:14:11.809
What's wrong, Yoshika?

00:14:14.312 --> 00:14:16.397
This is so sudden, though. Why Europe?

00:14:16.606 --> 00:14:17.398
Right!

00:14:17.607 --> 00:14:21.319
A new semester begins next month
at Helvetia's medical school.

00:14:21.527 --> 00:14:24.155
Apparently, they heard of your hopes
to enroll in a medical school,

00:14:24.364 --> 00:14:26.532
so they've offered you an invitation.

00:14:26.741 --> 00:14:27.617
Wow!

00:14:27.825 --> 00:14:31.662
Yoshika! Helvetia is at the forefront
of the medical world!

00:14:31.871 --> 00:14:33.289
Oh! Really?

00:14:33.498 --> 00:14:36.834
Yes! It has one of the three finest
medical schools in Europe!

00:14:39.128 --> 00:14:40.671
I'll do it!

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:41.798
Yoshika...

00:14:42.006 --> 00:14:43.966
Are you really sure?

00:14:44.175 --> 00:14:48.054
Yeah! I'd love to study at
the forefront of medicine!

00:14:48.262 --> 00:14:50.473
Excellent! You should go, then!

00:14:50.681 --> 00:14:52.892
But, in exchange, be sure to study hard

00:14:53.101 --> 00:14:57.105
and master new Western medical
techniques before you return!

00:14:57.313 --> 00:14:59.982
I will! I promise!

00:14:59.982 --> 00:15:04.445
"August 3rd"
"Yokosuka Naval Base, Fuso Empire"

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:08.366
"Amagi Aircraft Carrier"

00:15:14.747 --> 00:15:18.251
Take care, everyone!

00:15:18.459 --> 00:15:20.336
Take good care of yourself!

00:15:20.545 --> 00:15:22.463
Study hard!

00:15:22.672 --> 00:15:25.591
Do your best, Yoshika!

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:28.469
See you later!

00:15:28.678 --> 00:15:31.472
See you later...!

00:15:40.982 --> 00:15:46.946
"The same day"
"Duchy of Venezia"

00:16:00.001 --> 00:16:03.754
"United States of Liberion,
Army Air Force Captain Charlotte E. Yeager"

00:16:03.754 --> 00:16:04.172
"Duchy of Romagna, Air Force Ensign Francesca
Lucchin This area has really recovered!

00:16:04.172 --> 00:16:05.715
"Duchy of Romagna,
Air Force Ensign Francesca Lucchini"

00:16:05.715 --> 00:16:06.382
Yeah!

00:16:06.591 --> 00:16:08.843
The bell tower's coming along, too!

00:16:09.844 --> 00:16:13.598
It's the city's symbol,
so I hope it gets fixed soon!

00:16:21.898 --> 00:16:23.483
It's the Regata Storica!

00:16:23.691 --> 00:16:26.027
The Regata what?

00:16:26.235 --> 00:16:29.947
It's a gondola speed race that starts next week!

00:16:31.782 --> 00:16:34.243
Speed race?

00:16:34.452 --> 00:16:37.580
It almost seemed like there
wouldn't be a Regata Storica this year!

00:16:37.788 --> 00:16:39.123
Right, Captain Fer?

00:16:39.332 --> 00:16:42.710
Yeah, the Neurois held
this area until just recently.

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:45.838
"504th Joint Fighter
Wing Ensign Luciana Mazzei"

00:16:45.838 --> 00:16:46.339
Martina. Could you please
stop rocking the gondola?

00:16:46.506 --> 00:16:50.259
"504th Joint Fighter
Wing Sergeant Martina Crespi"

00:16:50.259 --> 00:16:51.052
Victory will be ours again this year!

00:16:51.052 --> 00:16:54.722
"504th Joint Fighter
Wing Lieutenant Fernandia Malvezzi"

00:16:54.722 --> 00:16:55.681
Yep! We're unstoppable
when we have Luciana rowing!

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:58.476
I'm the fastest of all!

00:16:58.684 --> 00:17:00.186
Who's that?!

00:17:01.187 --> 00:17:03.606
--Hey, hey, hey!
--Fastest! Fastest!

00:17:03.814 --> 00:17:05.107
The 501 st?!

00:17:05.316 --> 00:17:07.818
It's Shirley and Lucchini!

00:17:08.027 --> 00:17:09.820
That's right!

00:17:10.029 --> 00:17:11.697
I challenge you, Redpants Squad!

00:17:11.906 --> 00:17:14.283
--What?!
--Bring it on!

00:17:14.492 --> 00:17:15.743
Wham?!

00:17:15.952 --> 00:17:18.621
Why does this always happen?!

00:17:18.829 --> 00:17:21.499
The Rialto Bridge is the goal!

00:17:21.707 --> 00:17:24.043
Show 'em who's boss, Luciana!
Captain's orders!

00:17:24.252 --> 00:17:26.629
H-Here goes!

00:17:26.837 --> 00:17:28.839
That's more like it!

00:17:33.135 --> 00:17:35.555
Ha ha! Spankety-spankety!

00:17:35.763 --> 00:17:37.598
Grr!

00:17:37.807 --> 00:17:38.641
Shirley!

00:17:38.849 --> 00:17:42.103
Huh. You're pretty good.

00:17:43.145 --> 00:17:44.855
Whoa, you're persistent.

00:17:45.064 --> 00:17:46.732
Come on, Luciana!

00:17:46.941 --> 00:17:48.985
Please keep still!

00:17:52.196 --> 00:17:54.574
This is bad, Captain Fer! What do we do?!

00:17:54.782 --> 00:17:57.034
Luciana! Activate magic power!

00:17:57.243 --> 00:17:59.579
Huh?! But that's against the rules!

00:17:59.787 --> 00:18:01.163
Captain's orders!

00:18:01.372 --> 00:18:04.041
Now hurry "P!

00:18:09.505 --> 00:18:11.465
They're cheating!

00:18:11.674 --> 00:18:12.758
You jerks!

00:18:12.967 --> 00:18:15.052
If that's how you wanna play...!

00:18:19.432 --> 00:18:21.726
Go, Shirley!

00:18:21.934 --> 00:18:23.686
All right!

00:18:23.894 --> 00:18:26.147
Fastest!

00:18:26.355 --> 00:18:27.857
So fast!

00:18:37.199 --> 00:18:38.576
We win!

00:18:38.784 --> 00:18:40.286
Spank, spank!

00:18:41.287 --> 00:18:43.205
L-I can't stop!

00:18:55.134 --> 00:18:56.636
They went flying...

00:18:57.637 --> 00:18:59.764
Ouch!

00:18:59.972 --> 00:19:04.143
--You've grown.
--Whoa, that looks painful.

00:19:06.896 --> 00:19:09.315
That's one nasty bump.

00:19:09.523 --> 00:19:12.693
Perhaps you could treat her, Captain Fer?

00:19:13.694 --> 00:19:15.655
Just this once.

00:19:18.699 --> 00:19:20.743
That feels itchy...

00:19:20.951 --> 00:19:22.870
That's how healing magic always feels.

00:19:23.079 --> 00:19:24.372
Quit complaining.

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:27.541
But Yoshika's magic never itched.

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:30.711
Oh, that's right. It never did.

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:35.675
Miyafuji's healing magic
also worked instantly, as I recall.

00:19:35.883 --> 00:19:37.677
Are you trying to hurt my feelings?

00:19:37.885 --> 00:19:40.012
N-No! I didn't mean it like that!

00:19:40.221 --> 00:19:41.555
I'm just joking.

00:19:41.764 --> 00:19:45.976
There aren't many people with
healing magic as strong as Miyafuji's!

00:19:46.185 --> 00:19:52.108
I heard she used up all her magic power
during the recent Operation Mars.

00:19:54.527 --> 00:19:58.906
It's thanks to her that we can hold
a Regata Storica this year.

00:20:02.618 --> 00:20:05.996
I wonder what she's up to now...

00:20:07.289 --> 00:20:09.583
Oh! It's all better!

00:20:09.792 --> 00:20:12.294
Well done, Captain Fer!

00:20:12.503 --> 00:20:14.255
It still itches!

00:20:14.463 --> 00:20:16.507
Quit being fussy!

00:20:16.716 --> 00:20:19.176
Good for you, Lucchini!

00:20:20.886 --> 00:20:22.388
It can't be!

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:25.307
A Neuroi?!

00:20:25.516 --> 00:20:26.517
No way!

00:20:26.726 --> 00:20:30.062
--How?!
--But we cleared out this entire area!

00:20:30.271 --> 00:20:32.064
What were the lookouts doing?!

00:20:32.273 --> 00:20:34.734
Captain Fer! I can't contact the base!

00:20:34.942 --> 00:20:35.776
What?!

00:20:35.985 --> 00:20:36.777
Lucchini!

00:20:36.986 --> 00:20:38.487
Right!

00:20:43.409 --> 00:20:45.870
Oh! Striker Units!

00:20:46.078 --> 00:20:48.581
"Always be prepared," y'know?

00:21:13.773 --> 00:21:15.357
Let's get going, too!

00:21:15.566 --> 00:21:17.193
We didn't bring any Units.

00:21:17.401 --> 00:21:18.444
Argh!

00:21:18.652 --> 00:21:20.237
Let's just go!

00:21:21.405 --> 00:21:22.198
Lucchini.

00:21:22.406 --> 00:21:25.701
Comms are on the fritz. Try to keep close.

00:21:31.999 --> 00:21:33.167
All right! Let's do it!

00:21:33.375 --> 00:21:34.877
R°gefl

00:21:39.423 --> 00:21:41.509
Cease fire!

00:21:41.717 --> 00:21:44.136
Witches! Witch reinforcements!

00:22:07.535 --> 00:22:10.454
That's it, Lucchini! Drive it out to sea!

00:22:10.663 --> 00:22:12.164
Got it!

00:22:29.014 --> 00:22:30.474
All right! It fell for it!

00:22:30.683 --> 00:22:31.851
Let's do it, Lucchini!

00:22:32.059 --> 00:22:33.561
R°gefl

00:22:34.603 --> 00:22:36.105
Gotcha!

00:22:37.606 --> 00:22:39.692
Below, Lucchini!

00:22:40.776 --> 00:22:41.735
There it is!

00:22:41.944 --> 00:22:44.280
--Wha...?!
--It transformed!

00:22:59.253 --> 00:23:01.505
This thing's tough!

00:23:05.843 --> 00:23:08.971
Hey! Hey!

00:23:12.308 --> 00:23:13.684
What is she doing?

00:23:13.893 --> 00:23:15.895
Shirley! Over there!

00:23:16.937 --> 00:23:18.564
Oh!

00:23:22.943 --> 00:23:25.362
Catch me if you can!

00:23:45.507 --> 00:23:46.592
There it is!

00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:48.344
The Rialto Bridge!

00:23:51.013 --> 00:23:53.515
--Here they come!
--Exactly as planned!

00:23:57.603 --> 00:23:59.647
You're not getting through here!

00:24:03.692 --> 00:24:05.194
It's all yours!

00:24:18.082 --> 00:24:19.541
We did it!

00:24:19.750 --> 00:24:22.336
What do you think?
This is all thanks to my plan!

00:24:22.544 --> 00:24:24.755
Nicely done, Captain Fer!

00:24:27.591 --> 00:24:29.009
Hey, Shirley.

00:24:29.218 --> 00:24:32.137
Where was that Neuroi hiding all this time?

00:24:33.514 --> 00:24:36.141
It was pretty tough for a straggler.

00:24:36.350 --> 00:24:39.103
There aren't any more, right?

00:24:39.311 --> 00:24:41.438
Let's hope not.

00:25:11.427 --> 00:25:13.137
Ensign Miyafuji...

00:25:14.930 --> 00:25:20.853
Me, getting to escort the famous
Ensign Miyafuji to Europe...

00:25:21.061 --> 00:25:25.649
Father. I'm going to accomplish
this assignment flawlessly!

00:25:27.776 --> 00:25:28.652
I'm back!

00:25:28.861 --> 00:25:30.904
O-Oh, welcome back!

00:25:31.113 --> 00:25:35.117
This is such a big ship! I got lost!

00:25:35.325 --> 00:25:38.203
The Amagi is 260 meters long.

00:25:38.412 --> 00:25:40.998
She's the largest of Fuso's aircraft carriers!

00:25:41.206 --> 00:25:44.752
Wow, you know a lot about ships, Ms. Hattori.

00:25:44.960 --> 00:25:46.253
You're like Michiko!

00:25:46.462 --> 00:25:49.798
Ensign Miyafujil, you needn't call me "Ms."!

00:25:50.007 --> 00:25:51.675
U-Uhh...

00:25:51.884 --> 00:25:54.553
Say, how old are you, Ms. Hattori?

00:25:54.762 --> 00:25:56.472
My age?

00:25:56.680 --> 00:25:58.223
I'm 14 years old.

00:25:58.432 --> 00:26:01.185
Wow, you're two years younger than me.

00:26:01.393 --> 00:26:04.938
You seemed so mature that
I assumed you were older than me.

00:26:05.147 --> 00:26:07.483
My apologies, Ensign!

00:26:07.691 --> 00:26:10.652
Umm, could you stop calling me that?

00:26:10.861 --> 00:26:13.739
I'm afraid I can't do that!
Military regulations!

00:26:13.947 --> 00:26:18.077
Oh, but Ms. Sakamoto told me long ago

00:26:18.285 --> 00:26:22.915
that since we're both in the navy,
we don't need to fuss over ranks.

00:26:23.123 --> 00:26:24.708
Major Sakamoto...?

00:26:24.917 --> 00:26:25.626
Yeah!

00:26:25.834 --> 00:26:30.089
So I'll call you, uhh, Shizuka.

00:26:30.297 --> 00:26:34.384
And you can call me Miya-Fuji
or Yoshika, whichever you like!

00:26:34.593 --> 00:26:38.889
A-All right, M-Ms. Miyafuji...

00:26:39.098 --> 00:26:40.224
That's better!

00:26:40.432 --> 00:26:44.603
Right! Ms... Miyafuji!

00:26:44.812 --> 00:26:47.481
I'll help you put your things away!

00:26:48.482 --> 00:26:51.318
All your personal belongings need
to be stored in these while on a ship.

00:26:51.527 --> 00:26:52.569
Military regulations.

00:26:52.778 --> 00:26:57.866
It's because belongings tend to pile up
over time, as I'm sure you know.

00:26:59.076 --> 00:27:01.120
Umm... Where are your things?

00:27:01.328 --> 00:27:03.580
Just this.

00:27:03.789 --> 00:27:04.873
That's it?

00:27:05.082 --> 00:27:07.126
You didn't, umm, bring anything else?

00:27:07.334 --> 00:27:08.293
Nope.

00:27:08.502 --> 00:27:11.547
But what about your uniforms?

00:27:11.755 --> 00:27:15.342
What about your first and
second military dresses?!

00:27:15.551 --> 00:27:16.802
I don't have any.

00:27:17.010 --> 00:27:18.679
Wham?!

00:27:21.431 --> 00:27:25.269
You didn't even bring your officer uniforms?

00:27:25.477 --> 00:27:28.438
Well, I'm not in the military anymore.

00:27:28.647 --> 00:27:29.982
That's not true now!

00:27:30.190 --> 00:27:34.319
You're going to be studying abroad
as an ensign in the Fuso Navy!

00:27:34.528 --> 00:27:38.740
A responsible, ranked military officer
<i>must</i> behave as such!

00:27:38.949 --> 00:27:40.450
Military regulations!

00:27:42.077 --> 00:27:43.829
I'm sorry...

00:28:09.229 --> 00:28:10.731
Ms. Miyafuji...

00:28:15.903 --> 00:28:18.238
I've finished chopping all the vegetables!

00:28:18.447 --> 00:28:19.740
Oh! That was fast!

00:28:19.948 --> 00:28:21.992
Could you fillet the mackerel too?

00:28:22.201 --> 00:28:24.995
Sure! Three pieces, right?

00:28:25.996 --> 00:28:26.997
MS. Miyafuii!

00:28:27.206 --> 00:28:28.457
Oh, Shizuka!

00:28:28.665 --> 00:28:32.628
Just wait a little longer!
Breakfast is almost ready!

00:28:32.836 --> 00:28:34.630
This won't do, Ms. Miyafuji!

00:28:34.838 --> 00:28:36.340
You're an officer, you know!

00:28:36.548 --> 00:28:39.551
As I told you, cooking is not your job!

00:28:39.760 --> 00:28:43.388
But we are all partners on the same ship...

00:28:43.597 --> 00:28:45.849
Even so, an officer is an officer!

00:28:46.058 --> 00:28:49.394
W-W-Wait! But the mackerel!

00:28:49.603 --> 00:28:51.688
It can stay where it is.

00:29:02.366 --> 00:29:03.867
<i>Take-off'.!</i>

00:29:08.497 --> 00:29:10.707
Hard left turn!

00:29:10.916 --> 00:29:12.459
MS. Miyafuii!

00:29:12.751 --> 00:29:14.753
"Navy Ramune"

00:29:19.424 --> 00:29:21.385
Oh! Ramune!

00:29:21.593 --> 00:29:23.470
Thank you!

00:29:31.311 --> 00:29:33.105
Yum!

00:29:34.773 --> 00:29:36.441
Ms. Miyafuji...

00:29:36.650 --> 00:29:39.528
Oh... Shizuka...

00:29:39.736 --> 00:29:41.780
Want some Ramune?

00:29:44.491 --> 00:29:47.077
The Naval Officer Regulations clearly state,

00:29:47.286 --> 00:29:50.455
"An officer is to act properly and
accordingly with one's standing;

00:29:50.664 --> 00:29:52.165
an ensign as an ensign,
a lieutenant as a lieutenant.

00:29:52.374 --> 00:29:55.335
In all matters, one's behavior
<i>must</i> match one's position."

00:29:55.544 --> 00:29:58.380
Military regulations! Rules!

00:29:58.588 --> 00:29:59.715
But...

00:29:59.923 --> 00:30:03.051
You're the finest of the Witches!
I've always looked up to you!

00:30:03.260 --> 00:30:04.761
<i>You're a hero of Fuse'.!</i>

00:30:04.970 --> 00:30:08.140
So you need to act as
a role model for everyone else!

00:30:08.348 --> 00:30:12.769
But I'm being shown such hospitality
that I thought I could at least help...

00:30:12.978 --> 00:30:16.815
Plus, I'm not a Witch anymore.

00:30:17.024 --> 00:30:19.318
I'm sorry.

00:30:19.526 --> 00:30:21.528
Even so, regulations are regulations!

00:30:21.737 --> 00:30:24.656
Upholding rules is a basic tenant
of the armed forces!

00:30:24.865 --> 00:30:27.743
The armed forces exist for a reason!

00:30:27.951 --> 00:30:32.664
I almost feel like Ms. Hartmann
being scolded by Ms. Barkhorn...

00:30:34.583 --> 00:30:38.420
"Karlsland Imperial Air Force
Lieutenant Erica Hartmann"

00:30:38.420 --> 00:30:38.503
Maintaining a proper health regimen

00:30:38.712 --> 00:30:41.506
is an essential duty of every
Karlsland soldier, you know.

00:30:41.506 --> 00:30:43.383
"Karlsland Imperial Air Force
Captain Gertrud Barkhorn"

00:30:43.383 --> 00:30:47.012
Being unable to fight in an emergency
because of a cold is absolutely impermissible!

00:30:47.220 --> 00:30:48.930
You should learn--

00:30:49.139 --> 00:30:51.725
Don't smear it on me!

00:30:53.268 --> 00:30:55.604
Do you understand?

00:30:55.812 --> 00:30:58.982
Then... what shouldl do?

00:30:59.191 --> 00:31:00.525
This.

00:31:00.734 --> 00:31:02.944
Study.

00:31:03.153 --> 00:31:05.113
R-Right!

00:31:14.373 --> 00:31:16.666
It's been three weeks since leaving Fuso.

00:31:16.875 --> 00:31:18.502
We're finally at Cape Town.

00:31:18.710 --> 00:31:19.753
Yeah.

00:31:19.961 --> 00:31:22.589
This is some heavy fog, though.

00:31:22.798 --> 00:31:25.217
I can't see our bow or anything ahead.

00:31:41.733 --> 00:31:44.444
Almost at the tip of Africa!

00:31:52.035 --> 00:31:53.078
An alarm?!

00:31:53.286 --> 00:31:54.079
Neurois?!

00:31:54.287 --> 00:31:57.666
No! Reports say we've collided
with a large iceberg!

00:31:57.874 --> 00:31:59.251
An iceberg?!

00:31:59.459 --> 00:32:00.710
What were the spotters doing?!

00:32:00.919 --> 00:32:03.672
Captain! A fire has broken out
near the auxiliary generator room!

00:32:03.880 --> 00:32:05.382
What?!

00:32:11.930 --> 00:32:12.806
The corridor!

00:32:13.014 --> 00:32:14.433
The fire is up ahead!

00:32:14.641 --> 00:32:17.477
Next to the ammunition room!
What happened to the extinguishers?!

00:32:17.686 --> 00:32:19.146
They don't work! They're disconnected!

00:32:19.354 --> 00:32:21.481
What?! What about the emergency valve?!

00:32:21.690 --> 00:32:23.066
It's on the other side!

00:32:23.275 --> 00:32:25.694
Chief Petty Officer Yuki is still there!

00:32:25.902 --> 00:32:27.863
Yuki! How does it look?!

00:32:28.071 --> 00:32:28.905
It's no good!

00:32:29.114 --> 00:32:32.284
The extinguisher valve won't turn
because of the collision!

00:32:32.492 --> 00:32:34.494
Damn! What can we do?!

00:32:34.703 --> 00:32:36.329
I apologize for my tardiness!

00:32:37.998 --> 00:32:40.959
This is the situation at hand. Can you help?

00:32:41.168 --> 00:32:42.669
I understand!

00:33:06.902 --> 00:33:07.861
It's no good!

00:33:08.069 --> 00:33:09.738
Yuki! Are you all right?!

00:33:09.946 --> 00:33:11.615
The fire's almost there!

00:33:11.823 --> 00:33:15.327
Close the watertight door and
flood this compartment with water!

00:33:15.535 --> 00:33:16.328
What?!

00:33:16.536 --> 00:33:18.121
Huh?!

00:33:18.330 --> 00:33:21.583
Please! Flood the compartment! Hurry!

00:33:21.791 --> 00:33:24.002
But then you'd be...!

00:33:24.211 --> 00:33:27.130
The ammunition will explode
unless we do something!

00:33:27.339 --> 00:33:29.549
Please hurry!

00:33:29.758 --> 00:33:31.676
Captain!

00:33:31.885 --> 00:33:34.721
He is the longest-serving officer on this ship.

00:33:34.930 --> 00:33:36.723
It's the only option.

00:33:37.807 --> 00:33:39.476
Flood it! Hurry!

00:33:41.102 --> 00:33:42.729
The captain has given his orders.

00:33:42.938 --> 00:33:45.941
We're to close the watertight door
and flood the compartment!

00:33:46.149 --> 00:33:47.734
Close the watertight door...

00:33:47.943 --> 00:33:49.444
Understood.

00:34:02.249 --> 00:34:04.793
I'm sorry, Yuki.

00:34:10.382 --> 00:34:11.216
MS. Miyafuii!

00:34:11.424 --> 00:34:13.635
Ms. Miyafuji! What are you doing?!

00:34:13.843 --> 00:34:14.886
Move aside!

00:34:15.095 --> 00:34:16.555
No, Ms. Miyafuji!

00:34:16.763 --> 00:34:18.473
The watertight door is closing!

00:34:18.682 --> 00:34:20.100
Someone's in there, right?!

00:34:20.308 --> 00:34:21.560
Captain's orders!

00:34:21.768 --> 00:34:23.395
So what?!

00:34:24.771 --> 00:34:26.273
MS. Miyafuii!

00:34:40.370 --> 00:34:43.999
Captain... I wish you luck...

00:34:44.207 --> 00:34:45.292
You can't give up!

00:34:45.500 --> 00:34:47.252
Ms. Miyafuji?!

00:34:48.920 --> 00:34:50.880
We can do this together!

00:34:52.465 --> 00:34:53.550
What's the situation?!

00:34:53.758 --> 00:34:55.343
Ammunition room temperature rising!

00:34:55.552 --> 00:34:58.138
Critical temperature
in approximately three minutes!

00:34:59.514 --> 00:35:01.683
Begin flooding it in two minutes.

00:35:01.891 --> 00:35:03.351
Understood.

00:35:03.560 --> 00:35:06.730
Please hurry, Ms. Miyafuji.

00:35:09.232 --> 00:35:12.152
It's no use, Ms. Miyafuji!

00:35:12.360 --> 00:35:13.653
It won't budge!

00:35:13.862 --> 00:35:16.031
No! You can't give up!

00:35:19.326 --> 00:35:22.412
It's been two minutes. Begin flooding.

00:35:26.082 --> 00:35:27.667
Ms. Miyafuji...

00:35:34.299 --> 00:35:35.300
Water!

00:35:35.508 --> 00:35:37.302
All right!

00:35:37.510 --> 00:35:39.012
They did it!

00:35:39.220 --> 00:35:41.097
I knew they'd do it!

00:35:55.945 --> 00:35:59.199
--Oh!
--They're both okay!

00:35:59.407 --> 00:36:00.784
<i>Ms. Nfiyafuffl. Yuk“.!</i>

00:36:00.992 --> 00:36:05.246
--You all right?!
--Thank you, Ms. Miyafuji!

00:36:05.455 --> 00:36:07.374
She's really something.

00:36:07.582 --> 00:36:10.919
--Thank you!
--Let's go!

00:36:24.015 --> 00:36:26.142
It sure is cold.

00:36:26.351 --> 00:36:30.063
I always expected Africa
to be a lot warmer than this.

00:36:34.234 --> 00:36:37.278
I'm sorry for yelling at you earlier.

00:36:37.487 --> 00:36:41.741
It's all right. But you were
wrong to do what you did.

00:36:41.950 --> 00:36:44.411
Why didn't you follow orders?

00:36:44.619 --> 00:36:45.745
<i>I'm sorry'.!</i>

00:36:45.954 --> 00:36:48.581
But at least everyone made it out okay.

00:36:48.790 --> 00:36:51.960
No! The ship could've sunk!

00:36:52.168 --> 00:36:54.713
The captain's orders hold absolute authority!

00:36:54.921 --> 00:36:58.758
It was just dumb luck that your plan worked!

00:36:58.967 --> 00:36:59.968
But...

00:37:00.176 --> 00:37:02.929
Orders are absolute!

00:37:07.142 --> 00:37:09.811
If you'll excuse me, Ensign Miyafuji.

00:37:20.447 --> 00:37:22.115
Shizuka...

00:38:04.949 --> 00:38:06.451
Land!

00:38:07.952 --> 00:38:09.162
At last.

00:38:09.370 --> 00:38:11.623
We've reached Pas-de-Calais!

00:38:18.713 --> 00:38:20.215
That sound...

00:38:22.926 --> 00:38:24.219
Witches!

00:38:24.427 --> 00:38:25.929
They're fast!

00:38:27.347 --> 00:38:31.100
Those engine sounds...
A Griffon 61 and a Quadra 12!

00:38:31.309 --> 00:38:32.477
Could it be...?!

00:38:32.685 --> 00:38:34.938
Lynne! Perrine!

00:38:34.938 --> 00:38:37.941
"Britannian Air Force
Master Sergeant Lynette Bishop"

00:38:38.107 --> 00:38:41.110
Lyme!

00:38:46.199 --> 00:38:49.202
I couldn't wait, so I flew straight here!

00:38:49.410 --> 00:38:52.163
I couldn't wait to see you, either!

00:38:54.040 --> 00:38:56.960
<i>Th-This</i> is Master Sergeant Lynette Bishop?!

00:38:57.168 --> 00:38:58.920
They haven't changed at all.

00:38:59.128 --> 00:39:01.339
It's only been two months, too.

00:39:01.548 --> 00:39:03.758
Huh?! A-Are you..,?!

00:39:04.759 --> 00:39:08.221
It's an honor to meet you,
Lieutenant Perrine Clostermann!

00:39:08.429 --> 00:39:12.809
<i>I'm Sergeant Hattofl Shizuka of the Fuse Navy'.!</i>

00:39:12.892 --> 00:39:16.688
"Gallian Air Force
Lieutenant Perrine Clostermann"

00:39:16.855 --> 00:39:20.191
You must be exhausted
after your time with Ms. Miyafuji.

00:39:20.400 --> 00:39:22.610
--N-No! Not at all!
--How have you been?

00:39:22.819 --> 00:39:25.113
Just great!

00:39:26.698 --> 00:39:28.825
I'm so glad!

00:39:34.914 --> 00:39:38.334
"Pas-de-Calais, Gallia"

00:39:52.223 --> 00:39:56.686
Wow. So you're escorting
her alone, Ms. Hattori?

00:39:56.895 --> 00:40:01.566
Yes. It was my father's idea,
to commemorate my 14th birthday.

00:40:01.774 --> 00:40:03.443
By the way, Ms. Miyafuji...

00:40:03.651 --> 00:40:06.529
ls Major Sakamoto doing well?

00:40:06.738 --> 00:40:10.617
H-Has she said anything about me, perhaps?

00:40:10.825 --> 00:40:14.454
Sorry. I haven't seen her, actually.

00:40:14.662 --> 00:40:19.417
I visited the base, but she was away
on an emergency mission.

00:40:19.626 --> 00:40:21.711
An emergency mission?

00:40:25.882 --> 00:40:29.010
Wow! Grapes!

00:40:29.218 --> 00:40:30.929
They look tasty!

00:40:31.137 --> 00:40:35.016
The grapes here are for wine, though.
They taste sour if you eat them.

00:40:35.224 --> 00:40:37.977
What do you think? Gallia's beautiful, isn't it?

00:40:38.186 --> 00:40:40.855
<i>Yes! It's really pretty!</i>

00:40:41.064 --> 00:40:44.359
This entire area belongs to Perrine, you know!

00:40:44.567 --> 00:40:45.401
Wow!

00:40:45.610 --> 00:40:47.612
Thank you for your hard work, everyone!

00:40:47.820 --> 00:40:48.738
Oh!

00:40:48.947 --> 00:40:50.531
A castle!

00:41:05.713 --> 00:41:10.969
Despite how it seems, it's in much better
shape now than right after the liberation.

00:41:14.847 --> 00:41:18.184
Welcome back, Perrine! Lynne!

00:41:18.393 --> 00:41:20.436
Welcome back, Ms. Perrine!

00:41:20.645 --> 00:41:22.814
Welcome back, Big Sis Perrine!

00:41:23.022 --> 00:41:25.066
It's almost time for class!

00:41:25.274 --> 00:41:28.111
Yes, I know. I did make it in time!

00:41:29.112 --> 00:41:31.948
Welcome back, Miss.

00:41:32.156 --> 00:41:34.993
I trust nothing happened while I was away?

00:41:35.201 --> 00:41:38.913
A senator has been waiting to see you.

00:41:40.873 --> 00:41:43.584
Could it wait until after class?

00:41:44.919 --> 00:41:46.671
I understand.

00:41:46.879 --> 00:41:49.048
Okay! Let's begin class!

00:41:49.257 --> 00:41:51.634
--Okay!
--Yeah!

00:41:51.843 --> 00:41:54.053
Hey! Over here!

00:41:54.262 --> 00:41:56.973
Who are those kids, Lynne?

00:41:57.181 --> 00:42:01.436
Children who lost their parents
during the fighting with the Neurois.

00:42:01.644 --> 00:42:05.732
Perrine took them in.
They all live together now.

00:42:21.039 --> 00:42:23.541
Now, who can answer this problem?

00:42:23.750 --> 00:42:24.417
<i>“Me!
“Me!</i>

00:42:24.625 --> 00:42:25.793
It's easy!

00:42:26.002 --> 00:42:27.503
Is it?

00:42:36.179 --> 00:42:39.974
You're amazing, Perrine!
You even know how to teach!

00:42:40.183 --> 00:42:45.772
As a girl from an aristocratic family,
this is the least of what I can do.

00:42:45.980 --> 00:42:50.860
I need to meet with someone now,
so might I ask you a favor?

00:42:51.069 --> 00:42:52.653
Sure. What is it?

00:42:52.862 --> 00:42:57.450
Could you make dinner
before the children grow tired?

00:42:57.658 --> 00:42:59.702
The three of you.

00:42:59.911 --> 00:43:02.663
--Sure!
--No problem!

00:43:02.872 --> 00:43:04.332
Cooking...?

00:43:04.540 --> 00:43:06.793
Is something the matter, Ms. Hattori?

00:43:07.001 --> 00:43:10.088
L-I-l will gladly help!

00:43:20.890 --> 00:43:22.934
Are you okay, Shizuka?

00:43:23.142 --> 00:43:24.977
L-I'm fine!

00:43:25.186 --> 00:43:27.438
Wow! This is Fuso food?!

00:43:27.647 --> 00:43:28.898
It looks good!

00:43:29.107 --> 00:43:30.858
Now, then. We gratefully accept this food.

00:43:31.067 --> 00:43:32.777
We gratefully accept this food!

00:43:32.985 --> 00:43:34.904
We gratefully accept!

00:43:36.948 --> 00:43:38.950
This tastes good!

00:43:41.202 --> 00:43:44.372
Wow! This <i>nikujaga</i> is just like the real thing!

00:43:44.580 --> 00:43:47.375
Thank you! Eat lots, okay?

00:43:49.085 --> 00:43:51.170
My, what a nice aroma!

00:43:51.379 --> 00:43:54.590
Did you make this miso soup, Ms. Hattori?

00:43:54.799 --> 00:43:57.593
L-I hope it's to your liking!

00:44:01.389 --> 00:44:05.351
Blech! What is this?! It's gross!

00:44:05.560 --> 00:44:07.019
Salty...

00:44:07.228 --> 00:44:09.689
Th-This is... miso soup?

00:44:12.483 --> 00:44:15.653
L-It certainly has a... unique flavor.

00:44:16.821 --> 00:44:20.533
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:44:46.017 --> 00:44:47.518
Huh?

00:44:58.946 --> 00:45:01.949
Feeling bad about dinner?

00:45:02.158 --> 00:45:03.326
Lieutenant!

00:45:03.534 --> 00:45:05.828
N-No! Well, yes!

00:45:06.037 --> 00:45:08.372
I apologize, Lieutenant!

00:45:12.835 --> 00:45:17.965
I used to think that cooking
was only for cooks, too.

00:45:18.174 --> 00:45:21.719
L, umm, come from a military family
that goes back generations.

00:45:21.928 --> 00:45:23.804
As such, I'm not very...

00:45:25.681 --> 00:45:28.351
You were born with the qualities to be a Witch.

00:45:28.559 --> 00:45:31.020
So you were raised with
the expectations of being a soldier,

00:45:31.229 --> 00:45:33.564
and had no time to cook?

00:45:33.773 --> 00:45:34.815
Correct.

00:45:35.024 --> 00:45:37.526
My family isn't a Witch family,

00:45:37.735 --> 00:45:40.863
so my father and grandfather
had very high expectations of me.

00:45:41.072 --> 00:45:43.449
If you were raised in an environment like that,

00:45:43.658 --> 00:45:47.411
it's understandable that Miyafuji
might rub you the wrong way.

00:45:47.620 --> 00:45:50.623
No, Ensign Miyafuji is the pride of Fuso!

00:45:50.831 --> 00:45:53.876
She's a heroic Witch
who helped liberate Europe!

00:45:54.877 --> 00:45:59.340
But she doesn't seem like
a heroic soldier, does she?

00:45:59.548 --> 00:46:03.678
She ignores regulations. She ignores orders.
She does whatever she wants.

00:46:03.886 --> 00:46:05.846
She's a real handful.

00:46:07.890 --> 00:46:10.393
"I don't like war."

00:46:11.394 --> 00:46:15.856
That's the first thing Ms. Miyafuji said
to us when she joined the 501 st.

00:46:16.065 --> 00:46:20.403
Even though the Neurois had been
laying waste to our homelands.

00:46:21.737 --> 00:46:26.575
She irritated me. I wondered why
she had even joined in the first place.

00:46:27.785 --> 00:46:29.453
But it was strange.

00:46:30.705 --> 00:46:36.419
Once she joined the 501st,
we grew even stronger.

00:46:37.920 --> 00:46:42.341
Without her, Gallia might
never have been freed.

00:46:43.676 --> 00:46:45.177
MN'

00:46:46.512 --> 00:46:48.681
Perplexed, yes?

00:46:48.889 --> 00:46:50.599
Well, good night.

00:46:50.808 --> 00:46:52.977
We have an early day tomorrow!

00:47:02.737 --> 00:47:05.781
Estimated arrival at 1800 hours. Over.

00:47:05.990 --> 00:47:08.492
This is HQ. Copy. Over.

00:47:08.701 --> 00:47:10.286
Roger and out.

00:47:11.746 --> 00:47:14.540
Rheims is about 200 kilometers
southeast of here.

00:47:14.749 --> 00:47:18.502
If you continue from there,
you'll reach Dijon by evening.

00:47:18.711 --> 00:47:20.880
That's where we plan to stay tonight.

00:47:21.088 --> 00:47:25.843
Stay clear of the border
to the east of the highway.

00:47:26.052 --> 00:47:29.513
If you cross the Rhine,
the Neurois will attack without mercy.

00:47:29.722 --> 00:47:31.223
I understand.

00:47:32.266 --> 00:47:34.268
Take this with you, Yoshika.

00:47:34.477 --> 00:47:36.062
Huh? What is it?

00:47:41.192 --> 00:47:43.402
A doctor's coat!

00:47:43.611 --> 00:47:45.988
Did you make this for me, Lynne?!

00:47:46.197 --> 00:47:50.618
Yeah! I heard you were going to be a doctor.

00:47:50.826 --> 00:47:52.370
Lynne. You're hurt...

00:47:52.578 --> 00:47:58.834
Oh, err... I'm still not very good at sewing.

00:47:59.043 --> 00:48:03.005
She's been working on it
for the past month straight!

00:48:03.214 --> 00:48:04.715
Thank you, Lynne!

00:48:04.924 --> 00:48:08.010
<i>I will</i> become a great doctor! I promise!

00:48:08.219 --> 00:48:09.929
Try your best, Yoshika!

00:48:10.137 --> 00:48:11.639
I will!

00:48:19.188 --> 00:48:21.649
I packed you a lunch. Eat it along the way!

00:48:21.857 --> 00:48:26.278
--Okay!
--This is St. John's wort from our herb garden.

00:48:26.487 --> 00:48:27.655
It heals wounds!

00:48:27.863 --> 00:48:31.492
Thank you, Lynne! Perrine!

00:48:31.700 --> 00:48:33.786
It's time to depart.

00:48:37.540 --> 00:48:40.084
Lynne! Perrine!

00:48:40.292 --> 00:48:41.585
See you later!

00:48:41.794 --> 00:48:46.465
Yoshika! I'll write to you!

00:48:54.306 --> 00:48:59.311
"Peterberg, Orussian Empire
502nd Joint Fighter Wing, Front Line Base"

00:49:00.271 --> 00:49:05.276
What's Nipa's problem? Too good
to say goodbye to her friends?

00:49:05.359 --> 00:49:08.279
"Orussian Imperial Army
Lieutenant Sanya V. Litvyak"

00:49:08.279 --> 00:49:10.072
You shouldn't say that. She's on an assignment.

00:49:10.072 --> 00:49:11.824
"Suomus Air Force
Lieutenant Eila llmatar Juutilainen"

00:49:11.824 --> 00:49:12.283
But, it's just...

00:49:14.535 --> 00:49:19.790
She's trying to finish her assignment
in time to see you off.

00:49:19.999 --> 00:49:21.375
Captain Sasha.

00:49:21.584 --> 00:49:23.794
Umm, thank you for everything.

00:49:24.003 --> 00:49:25.129
Thank you.

00:49:25.337 --> 00:49:26.672
Not at all.

00:49:26.672 --> 00:49:29.258
"502nd Joint Fighter Wing
Captain Aleksandra I. Pokryshkin"

00:49:29.258 --> 00:49:31.135
But the base is going to be
a lonely place without you.

00:49:31.343 --> 00:49:33.721
Hey!

00:49:33.929 --> 00:49:36.265
Heeey!

00:49:36.265 --> 00:49:39.226
"502nd Joint Fighter Wing
Sergeant Nikka Edvardine Katajainen"

00:49:39.226 --> 00:49:39.310
Hey!

00:49:39.518 --> 00:49:42.396
Ms. Nipa made it back, Eila!

00:49:42.605 --> 00:49:45.691
What a relief! It looks like
nothing happened today!

00:49:45.900 --> 00:49:48.944
No, it's still too soon to say...

00:49:55.576 --> 00:49:56.452
Oh, no!

00:49:56.660 --> 00:50:00.581
Sheesh. She's as unlucky as ever.

00:50:03.584 --> 00:50:05.836
Wrecked again, I see.

00:50:06.045 --> 00:50:08.839
That's the second time this month.

00:50:09.048 --> 00:50:12.218
We don't have the budget to keep this up.

00:50:12.426 --> 00:50:15.429
It's not like the lightning is my fault...

00:50:15.638 --> 00:50:18.557
The weather is worsening! Be careful!

00:50:21.268 --> 00:50:22.353
We will.

00:50:22.561 --> 00:50:25.272
We'll try to stay above the clouds.

00:50:25.481 --> 00:50:26.649
See you later, Nipa.

00:50:26.857 --> 00:50:28.817
Don't wreck any more.

00:50:34.657 --> 00:50:37.034
Eila... Ms. Sanya...

00:50:37.243 --> 00:50:39.245
MS.

00:50:39.453 --> 00:50:41.247
Hey!

00:50:41.455 --> 00:50:44.458
Be careful! Visit again sometime!

00:50:44.667 --> 00:50:46.544
Don't catch a cold!

00:50:47.878 --> 00:50:51.131
Watch out for lightning!

00:50:54.176 --> 00:50:56.929
See you!

00:51:23.664 --> 00:51:24.665
Are you cold?

00:51:24.873 --> 00:51:26.333
Just a little...

00:51:26.542 --> 00:51:28.919
Let's descend a bit.

00:51:47.896 --> 00:51:50.274
I hope 0l' Miyafuji is okay.

00:51:50.482 --> 00:51:52.776
Especially after what you saw
in your fortunetelling.

00:51:52.985 --> 00:51:57.239
You're the one who told me
to look into her future.

00:51:59.283 --> 00:52:00.492
The Tower...

00:52:00.701 --> 00:52:02.161
That's a bad omen.

00:52:02.369 --> 00:52:04.955
Miyafuji's in Gallia, right?

00:52:05.164 --> 00:52:07.541
Gallia should be Neuroi-free, though.

00:52:07.750 --> 00:52:09.710
Yeah.

00:52:11.670 --> 00:52:13.172
Huh?

00:52:14.590 --> 00:52:15.633
What's going on?

00:52:15.841 --> 00:52:18.135
--Eila!
--Huh?

00:52:18.344 --> 00:52:20.721
Wh-What is that?!

00:52:20.929 --> 00:52:23.557
Is it... a Neuroi?

00:52:34.818 --> 00:52:38.656
Say, you should have some too. It's tasty!

00:52:38.864 --> 00:52:39.782
No, thank you.

00:52:39.990 --> 00:52:42.451
I'm busy checking our route.

00:52:52.419 --> 00:52:54.046
What's this?

00:52:54.254 --> 00:52:56.715
Soldiers! Could I borrow your radio?!

00:52:56.924 --> 00:52:58.759
Huh? What's the matter?

00:52:58.967 --> 00:53:02.346
My village was hit by a landslide!
Many people were hurt!

00:53:02.554 --> 00:53:04.181
--A landslide?!
--Oh, no!

00:53:04.390 --> 00:53:07.017
I tried to call for help,
but the phones are down!

00:53:07.226 --> 00:53:09.645
--Shizuka!
--Understood!

00:53:13.315 --> 00:53:15.317
Huh? The radio isn't working.

00:53:15.526 --> 00:53:17.361
It was working fine when we left...

00:53:17.569 --> 00:53:21.365
I can give them basic treatment! Take me there!

00:53:21.573 --> 00:53:23.742
Y-You're a doctor?!

00:53:23.951 --> 00:53:26.787
No, Ensign! The village is near the border!

00:53:26.995 --> 00:53:28.956
Lieutenant Perrine said we need to avoid it!

00:53:29.164 --> 00:53:31.333
Let's go, Shizuka!

00:53:31.542 --> 00:53:33.127
Ensign...

00:53:46.557 --> 00:53:48.058
This way!

00:53:53.564 --> 00:53:54.690
This is terrible...

00:53:54.898 --> 00:53:57.401
We need to stop the bleeding quickly.

00:53:57.609 --> 00:54:00.446
Perrine's herbs should work.

00:54:00.654 --> 00:54:01.947
I'll also need...

00:54:02.156 --> 00:54:04.032
Do you have any bandages?

00:54:04.241 --> 00:54:07.035
Actually, we've used up all that we have...

00:54:07.244 --> 00:54:09.538
Any clean sheets or towels?

00:54:09.747 --> 00:54:12.082
There's nothing left.

00:54:22.134 --> 00:54:24.428
Sorry, Lynne.

00:54:43.906 --> 00:54:45.866
Everyone pulled through, thanks to you.

00:54:46.074 --> 00:54:48.619
You really saved the day!

00:54:59.379 --> 00:55:01.840
Oh, it's already night.

00:55:04.718 --> 00:55:07.012
Have you contacted the base?

00:55:07.221 --> 00:55:09.348
It's no use. There's too much interference.

00:55:09.556 --> 00:55:14.853
I can't raise the St. Trond,
Sedan, or Dijon bases at all.

00:55:15.062 --> 00:55:16.855
I wonder if it's broken...

00:55:17.064 --> 00:55:20.484
It functioned perfectly fine when we left.

00:55:20.692 --> 00:55:22.569
The village's phones are down, too.

00:55:22.778 --> 00:55:26.532
It's getting late. You can stay here tonight.

00:55:27.533 --> 00:55:29.117
Thank you!

00:55:29.326 --> 00:55:30.994
Shizuka! Let's accept!

00:55:31.203 --> 00:55:35.624
I'd like to, but we haven't completed
even one regular check-in today.

00:55:35.833 --> 00:55:39.336
Aww. Can't we do that tomorrow?

00:55:39.545 --> 00:55:41.547
It's our duty to report our activities.

00:55:41.755 --> 00:55:43.924
You can go on ahead, Ensign.

00:55:50.514 --> 00:55:54.309
"St. Trond Base, Belgica Kingdom"

00:56:00.065 --> 00:56:01.608
Sign here, please.

00:56:01.817 --> 00:56:05.320
Still, half a month since
your last supply delivery?

00:56:05.320 --> 00:56:07.823
"Karlsland Imperial Air Force
Lieutenant Colonel Mina Dietlinde Wilcke"

00:56:07.823 --> 00:56:08.073
It's a good thing that we're not busy.

00:56:08.282 --> 00:56:10.701
The rest of the front line's the same way, too.

00:56:10.909 --> 00:56:13.662
I'd love things to stay like this.

00:56:13.871 --> 00:56:15.706
Indeed.

00:56:15.914 --> 00:56:17.708
I'll be off now.

00:56:17.916 --> 00:56:19.418
Thank you.

00:56:26.800 --> 00:56:28.302
Oww!

00:56:29.553 --> 00:56:32.180
I broke my nail...

00:56:32.389 --> 00:56:36.643
I can't feel my hands anymore!
This is such a pain! No more! No more!

00:56:36.852 --> 00:56:39.605
That's what you get for losing your loader.

00:56:39.813 --> 00:56:41.857
No! This is just too tough!

00:56:42.065 --> 00:56:46.570
You just have to go... like this... It's easy!

00:56:46.778 --> 00:56:48.113
When you're as strong as a troll...

00:56:48.322 --> 00:56:49.531
Come again?!

00:56:49.740 --> 00:56:52.868
How do you even lose
a loader in the first place?!

00:56:53.076 --> 00:56:58.332
Securing and inspecting your weapon is
the most basic rule for any Karlsland soldier!

00:57:01.460 --> 00:57:04.087
You have a call, Lieutenant Colonel Mina.

00:57:05.422 --> 00:57:08.800
I see. A Neuroi appeared in Venezia, too?

00:57:09.009 --> 00:57:11.094
There are no hives within 200 miles,

00:57:11.303 --> 00:57:14.181
and lookouts on Romagna's borders
haven't picked up anything.

00:57:14.389 --> 00:57:16.600
Where could it have come from?

00:57:16.808 --> 00:57:18.644
It is disconcerting.

00:57:18.852 --> 00:57:22.230
Continue your joint
surveillance with the 504th.

00:57:22.439 --> 00:57:23.941
R°gefl

00:57:26.568 --> 00:57:30.113
First Belgica, then Venezia.

00:57:32.115 --> 00:57:38.080
The closest hives are in Berlin,
Nuremberg, and Prague.

00:57:38.288 --> 00:57:40.582
The Neurois' spheres of action are...

00:57:43.293 --> 00:57:44.753
That's odd.

00:57:44.962 --> 00:57:47.589
The hives are too far away.

00:57:47.798 --> 00:57:49.424
Tell me about the Neuroi you saw.

00:57:49.633 --> 00:57:52.010
Right. It was a single, mid-sized unit,

00:57:52.219 --> 00:57:55.222
located south of this base
and headed northwest.

00:57:55.430 --> 00:57:57.975
So it wasn't a normal scout, then?

00:57:58.183 --> 00:58:00.560
Its mobility and firepower
were on a different level,

00:58:00.769 --> 00:58:02.729
and it was shaped like nothing I'd seen before.

00:58:02.938 --> 00:58:04.314
I see.

00:58:04.523 --> 00:58:08.068
It seems to match the one in Shirley's report.

00:58:08.276 --> 00:58:10.862
Could they have come from the same hive?

00:58:11.071 --> 00:58:14.324
Venezia is 800 kilometers
from here as the crow flies.

00:58:14.533 --> 00:58:16.702
I can't rule it out.

00:58:16.910 --> 00:58:18.412
But...

00:58:19.413 --> 00:58:21.707
There are no hives on that direct line.

00:58:21.915 --> 00:58:28.672
Plus, the border lookouts never detected
the one you encountered or the one in Venezia.

00:58:28.880 --> 00:58:33.510
They're not only out of range, but they
also slipped through our surveillance?

00:58:33.719 --> 00:58:36.430
Is there a new hive somewhere?

00:58:36.638 --> 00:58:38.765
We'll need to investigate.

00:58:38.974 --> 00:58:40.225
Investigate?

00:58:40.434 --> 00:58:42.561
I bet the surveillance team slipped up!

00:58:42.769 --> 00:58:45.522
I don't see why we should conduct recon!

00:58:45.731 --> 00:58:49.484
The surveillance team has been growing
far too lax when it comes to--

00:58:49.693 --> 00:58:51.153
Oh!

00:58:51.361 --> 00:58:54.948
Isn't Miyafuji going through here on her trip?

00:58:59.244 --> 00:59:00.746
Engines on!

00:59:01.872 --> 00:59:03.498
RPM is good!

00:59:03.707 --> 00:59:08.587
Starten auf! Direkteinspritzer
ready for takeoff!

00:59:08.795 --> 00:59:12.049
Is this "Ms. Miyafuji" the Ms. Miyafuji?

00:59:12.257 --> 00:59:15.469
Yes. She's Captain Barkhorn's
adorable little sister.

00:59:15.677 --> 00:59:17.095
Huh? Sister?

00:59:17.304 --> 00:59:20.223
Don't say misleading things like that, Mina!

00:59:20.432 --> 00:59:24.019
And don't take her joke seriously,
Major Heidemarie!

00:59:24.227 --> 00:59:26.229
I'm going on ahead, Big Sis!

00:59:26.438 --> 00:59:28.106
Hold on, Hartmann!

00:59:43.789 --> 00:59:45.248
We're almost to the Rhine.

00:59:45.457 --> 00:59:46.666
Stay sharp.

00:59:46.875 --> 00:59:50.629
But this side of the river is outside
the Neurois' range of activity.

00:59:50.837 --> 00:59:52.297
There's no danger here.

00:59:52.506 --> 00:59:54.674
That's what we're here to investigate.

00:59:54.883 --> 00:59:56.384
I Kay.

01:00:01.306 --> 01:00:03.975
The Karlsland side is in shambles.

01:00:04.184 --> 01:00:07.646
We can't get close, even though
it's just across the river...

01:00:07.854 --> 01:00:10.065
And it's our own country, too.

01:00:11.191 --> 01:00:14.694
We <i>will</i> take back our homeland
from the Neurois someday!

01:00:14.903 --> 01:00:17.155
Yeah! We will!

01:00:22.702 --> 01:00:25.080
Doesn't seem to be anything.

01:00:25.288 --> 01:00:27.124
We can probably head back.

01:00:27.332 --> 01:00:30.168
No. Let's continue south to the Loreley.

01:00:30.377 --> 01:00:31.878
Aww...

01:00:48.770 --> 01:00:50.355
I'm hungry»-

01:00:50.564 --> 01:00:52.816
Let's go back! Let's go back! Let's go back!

01:00:53.024 --> 01:00:55.277
Yes. I guess it's time to head back.

01:00:55.485 --> 01:00:57.696
Huh? Hooray!

01:00:57.904 --> 01:01:00.574
Sheesh. Why are you always so--

01:01:00.782 --> 01:01:02.534
Trude! Over there!

01:01:04.661 --> 01:01:06.788
--A Neuroi!
--From under the ground?!

01:01:06.997 --> 01:01:08.540
This is new!

01:01:12.377 --> 01:01:14.004
These are the ones Mina described!

01:01:14.212 --> 01:01:15.380
Let's do it, Hartmann!

01:01:15.589 --> 01:01:17.090
R°gefl

01:01:41.907 --> 01:01:42.949
We got it!

01:01:43.158 --> 01:01:44.743
That's one down!

01:01:49.414 --> 01:01:50.916
Get off me!

01:01:56.546 --> 01:01:58.173
A transforming type!

01:01:59.841 --> 01:02:01.343
Oh, no! It jammed!

01:02:17.025 --> 01:02:18.443
I'm hungry»-

01:02:18.652 --> 01:02:20.153
Just endure it!

01:02:38.546 --> 01:02:40.048
Now!

01:02:49.599 --> 01:02:50.809
I'm beat...

01:02:51.017 --> 01:02:53.228
That chimney one is still left.

01:02:53.436 --> 01:02:55.021
That-a-way.

01:02:55.230 --> 01:02:58.024
L-It crossed the Rhine?!

01:02:58.233 --> 01:03:00.318
I can't fight anymore.

01:03:00.527 --> 01:03:03.863
I'm out of ammo and magic.

01:03:04.072 --> 01:03:05.573
Picus! Do you read me?!

01:03:05.782 --> 01:03:06.908
This is Veiss-Fiinf!

01:03:07.117 --> 01:03:08.660
Do you read me, Mina?!

01:03:08.868 --> 01:03:11.913
Neuroi on the move at grid position G-14!

01:03:12.122 --> 01:03:13.498
It's breached the Rhine!

01:03:13.707 --> 01:03:15.208
<i>L</i> repeat“!

01:03:18.169 --> 01:03:20.380
There it goes.

01:03:21.381 --> 01:03:23.091
Damn! I can't get through!

01:03:23.300 --> 01:03:25.135
What is this?

01:03:25.343 --> 01:03:27.721
Is this why?!

01:03:27.929 --> 01:03:29.055
Let's hurry back!

01:03:29.264 --> 01:03:31.141
I'm out of strength...

01:03:31.349 --> 01:03:33.852
Sheesh. Why are you always so--?

01:03:39.399 --> 01:03:40.859
I can't go on...

01:03:41.067 --> 01:03:42.694
I'm starving...

01:03:42.902 --> 01:03:44.404
Hang in there, Hartmann.

01:03:44.612 --> 01:03:48.199
--Can't! I'm dying!
--You are not!

01:03:48.408 --> 01:03:49.909
Honestly, now!

01:03:54.164 --> 01:03:55.457
Eat this.

01:03:55.665 --> 01:03:56.624
Chocolate!

01:03:56.833 --> 01:03:58.335
Ya)!

01:03:59.627 --> 01:04:01.379
Here! For you!

01:04:01.588 --> 01:04:03.298
I don't need any. Take it all.

01:04:03.506 --> 01:04:06.301
Huh? Really?! Yay!

01:04:10.638 --> 01:04:12.390
That wasn't all of them?!

01:04:12.599 --> 01:04:13.975
Yikes! Here it comes!

01:04:14.184 --> 01:04:17.354
This is bad! I don't have
any weapons or magic left!

01:04:19.481 --> 01:04:20.774
Hartmann!

01:04:20.982 --> 01:04:22.859
Yummy chocolate!

01:04:30.700 --> 01:04:32.202
Hartmann!

01:04:38.291 --> 01:04:39.793
Sturm!

01:04:48.134 --> 01:04:50.470
I never even considered that method...

01:04:51.596 --> 01:04:52.555
Oh, no!

01:04:52.764 --> 01:04:55.850
Don't fall asleep! Wake up, Hartmann!

01:04:57.227 --> 01:04:59.562
Huh? Why are you here, Mina?

01:04:59.771 --> 01:05:03.108
I was worried when we suddenly lost contact!

01:05:03.316 --> 01:05:04.692
Mina!

01:05:04.901 --> 01:05:07.904
The Neurois have breached the border!

01:05:12.575 --> 01:05:14.994
Breakfast was great, wasn't it?!

01:05:15.203 --> 01:05:16.246
Yes.

01:05:16.454 --> 01:05:18.498
Is the radio fixed?

01:05:18.706 --> 01:05:20.208
No.

01:05:21.334 --> 01:05:23.795
We'll reach Helvetia tonight, right?

01:05:24.003 --> 01:05:25.004
Yes.

01:05:25.213 --> 01:05:27.841
Are you're going to leave after that?

01:05:28.049 --> 01:05:31.511
My assignment is to deliver you
to your destination.

01:05:32.595 --> 01:05:34.681
That makes me kind of sad...

01:05:38.351 --> 01:05:39.853
Stop the car!

01:05:49.863 --> 01:05:50.738
Those are...!

01:05:50.947 --> 01:05:51.781
Neurois!

01:05:51.990 --> 01:05:54.075
I'll contact the nearest base!

01:06:00.290 --> 01:06:01.624
I can't radio out!

01:06:01.833 --> 01:06:04.502
We should flee at once
to the nearby Bastogne base!

01:06:04.711 --> 01:06:06.546
No! Hurry to the village!

01:06:06.754 --> 01:06:08.047
It's too dangerous, Ensign!

01:06:08.256 --> 01:06:10.216
I'll evacuate everyone!

01:06:10.425 --> 01:06:13.261
You need to buy us some time!

01:06:13.470 --> 01:06:15.305
M-Me?!

01:06:53.301 --> 01:06:55.220
Ammunition loaded.

01:06:55.428 --> 01:06:56.221
Confirmed.

01:06:56.429 --> 01:06:58.723
Safety off!

01:06:58.723 --> 01:06:58.932
"Fire"
"Safety"

01:07:00.600 --> 01:07:03.353
I'll be fine, if I just follow my training!

01:07:03.561 --> 01:07:07.398
Hold the rifle steady with your shoulder...

01:07:07.607 --> 01:07:12.111
Close in on it, until it
won't fit in your sights...

01:07:12.320 --> 01:07:16.199
Place the upper part of your
index finger on the trigger...

01:07:16.407 --> 01:07:19.035
...and pull it straight...

01:07:19.244 --> 01:07:20.745
...back!

01:07:24.624 --> 01:07:27.585
I did it! Just like I trained!

01:07:34.884 --> 01:07:38.471
Stay strong! We're almost
to the air-raid shelter!

01:07:38.680 --> 01:07:41.266
Wow! Neurois aren't so tough!

01:07:42.767 --> 01:07:44.561
That's the last one.

01:07:45.687 --> 01:07:46.896
<i>L</i> 901: it!

01:07:47.105 --> 01:07:48.606
A big one!

01:07:50.650 --> 01:07:52.819
Huh?! It transformed!

01:08:11.796 --> 01:08:13.298
Shizuka!

01:08:18.845 --> 01:08:20.138
Shizuka! Say something!

01:08:20.346 --> 01:08:21.848
Shizuka!

01:08:22.932 --> 01:08:24.684
E-Ensign...

01:08:24.892 --> 01:08:27.645
Can you stand?! Let's evacuate to--

01:08:39.365 --> 01:08:43.369
"Republic of Gallia"
"506th Joint Fighter Wing, Sedan Base"

01:08:49.292 --> 01:08:51.210
All able-bodied Witches are to take off!

01:08:51.210 --> 01:08:53.129
"506th Joint Fighter Wing Major
Heinrike Prinzessin zu Sayn-Wittgenstein"

01:08:53.338 --> 01:08:54.881
Ms. Heinrike!

01:08:54.881 --> 01:08:58.259
"506th Joint Fighter Wing
Major Rosalie de Hemricourt de Grunne"

01:08:58.259 --> 01:08:58.635
I'll handle things here!
Please head into battle, too!

01:08:58.843 --> 01:09:00.470
Have you contacted the Dijon base?!

01:09:00.678 --> 01:09:02.388
It's no good! I can't reach it at all!

01:09:02.597 --> 01:09:04.724
Could it have been taken out?!

01:09:04.724 --> 01:09:07.644
"Ardnennes, Eastern Belgica"

01:09:22.367 --> 01:09:25.244
" Bastogne, Southern Belgica "

01:09:28.956 --> 01:09:30.625
This is Bastogne E Company!

01:09:30.833 --> 01:09:31.709
Please respond!

01:09:31.918 --> 01:09:34.003
This is Bastogne E Company!

01:09:37.507 --> 01:09:40.385
"Allied Forces, Western Headquarters"

01:09:40.385 --> 01:09:40.843
Neurois in Malmedy and Clervaux?!

01:09:41.052 --> 01:09:43.930
We've lost contact with the 506th in Sedan!

01:09:44.138 --> 01:09:45.973
Contact lost with Biillingen!

01:09:46.057 --> 01:09:49.143
"Supreme Commander of Liberion Expeditionary
Forces General Donald D. Eisenhower"

01:09:49.143 --> 01:09:49.936
Send the 101 st Airborne Division to Bastogne!

01:09:50.144 --> 01:09:52.146
Just what is happening?!

01:09:53.356 --> 01:09:55.608
<i>“St. Trend Base“</i>

01:09:56.984 --> 01:09:59.904
The Neurois' numbers
have increased even more.

01:10:00.113 --> 01:10:01.280
This is bad.

01:10:01.489 --> 01:10:03.366
The enemy has us surrounded.

01:10:03.574 --> 01:10:07.245
If this keeps up, all of
the Allied forces on the front line

01:10:07.453 --> 01:10:09.706
will end up surrounded, too.

01:10:09.914 --> 01:10:12.083
What is HQ doing?!

01:10:12.291 --> 01:10:14.502
The enemy is jamming our communications.

01:10:14.711 --> 01:10:16.921
We can't organize a retaliation strategy.

01:10:17.130 --> 01:10:19.173
Wired communications are down, too.

01:10:19.382 --> 01:10:23.594
I never imagined they'd dig underground
to breach our border surveillance!

01:10:23.803 --> 01:10:27.682
It's almost like the strategy we used on Malta.

01:10:27.890 --> 01:10:29.726
What do we do, Mina?

01:10:29.934 --> 01:10:34.021
Given the scale of this attack,
there's either a new hive somewhere

01:10:34.230 --> 01:10:38.818
or a Neuroi mothership
carrying smaller Neurois.

01:10:40.236 --> 01:10:41.154
Terrible news!

01:10:41.362 --> 01:10:43.656
We've lost contact with Yoshika!

01:10:43.865 --> 01:10:45.408
What?!

01:10:56.961 --> 01:11:00.506
It's going for the air-raid shelter!
I need to draw it away!

01:11:35.249 --> 01:11:36.584
Over here!

01:11:41.172 --> 01:11:42.673
I got its attention!

01:12:43.234 --> 01:12:44.986
It left...

01:12:47.947 --> 01:12:49.615
What a relief.

01:14:06.484 --> 01:14:08.277
Ensign Miyafuji...

01:14:34.345 --> 01:14:35.388
Ensign!

01:14:35.596 --> 01:14:37.807
Please pull yourself together, Ensign!

01:14:47.274 --> 01:14:49.151
Shizuka...

01:14:49.360 --> 01:14:50.903
What happened to the Neuroi?

01:14:52.279 --> 01:14:54.240
And the village?

01:14:54.448 --> 01:14:59.704
The village is safe!
Everyone is alive, thanks to you!

01:14:59.912 --> 01:15:04.208
That's good... I'm glad...

01:15:04.417 --> 01:15:07.044
Ensign! Ensign Miyafuji!

01:15:39.994 --> 01:15:41.746
There are so many of them...

01:15:44.248 --> 01:15:48.294
This is Hattori Shizuka.
Currently near St. Vith.

01:15:48.502 --> 01:15:52.131
Ensign Miyafuji seriously injured
during Neuroi attack.

01:15:52.339 --> 01:15:54.300
Emergency aid requested!

01:15:54.508 --> 01:15:57.636
I repeat, this is Hattori Shizuka!

01:15:59.180 --> 01:16:00.723
Why...?

01:16:00.931 --> 01:16:03.059
Why can't I get through?!

01:16:05.144 --> 01:16:07.521
Is it this?

01:16:07.730 --> 01:16:10.191
Are the Neurois jamming the signal?!

01:16:11.192 --> 01:16:12.693
Ensign!

01:16:25.414 --> 01:16:27.708
Just hang on, Ensign Miyafuji.

01:16:27.917 --> 01:16:29.835
<i>I will</i> return for you!

01:16:39.470 --> 01:16:40.763
Is this the place, Mina?!

01:16:40.971 --> 01:16:44.350
Yes. It's the center of where
the Neurois have been appearing.

01:16:44.558 --> 01:16:45.434
Stay alert!

01:16:45.643 --> 01:16:48.854
This is some serious
radio interference, I have to say.

01:16:49.063 --> 01:16:51.816
Is the enemy behind this, too?

01:16:52.024 --> 01:16:57.238
Yes. They're likely trying to disrupt our
communications and cut off our supplies.

01:16:57.446 --> 01:17:01.033
Please be all right, Yoshika...

01:17:01.242 --> 01:17:04.411
Your antenna is our
only hope, Major Heidemarie.

01:17:04.620 --> 01:17:09.500
R-R-Right. I understand.

01:17:09.708 --> 01:17:10.835
This is--

01:17:11.043 --> 01:17:14.004
Umm, I'm picking up a faint voice.

01:17:14.213 --> 01:17:15.297
A voice?

01:17:15.506 --> 01:17:19.093
--What is it saying?!
--I can't tell. There's too much interference.

01:17:22.054 --> 01:17:24.932
If I increase altitude and
get above the Neurois' jamming,

01:17:25.141 --> 01:17:27.309
I should be able to make radio contact!

01:17:34.859 --> 01:17:37.319
Anyone! Please respond!

01:17:37.528 --> 01:17:38.904
This is Hattori Shizuka!

01:17:39.113 --> 01:17:40.948
Please respond!

01:17:42.825 --> 01:17:43.951
Please...

01:17:44.160 --> 01:17:46.287
Someone answer me...

01:17:46.495 --> 01:17:49.498
Save Ensign Miyafuji!

01:17:49.707 --> 01:17:52.084
I have a signal! Routing to you!

01:17:53.752 --> 01:17:57.715
Please! Save Ensign Miyafuji!

01:17:57.923 --> 01:17:58.883
Ms. Miyafuji?!

01:17:59.091 --> 01:17:59.884
Miyafuii!

01:18:00.092 --> 01:18:00.885
Miyafuji?!

01:18:01.093 --> 01:18:01.927
MS. Miyafuii!

01:18:02.136 --> 01:18:03.637
Yoshika!

01:18:04.889 --> 01:18:06.098
Miyafuii!

01:18:06.307 --> 01:18:07.850
Yoshika!

01:18:11.478 --> 01:18:12.980
Miyafuii!

01:18:15.065 --> 01:18:16.567
Yoshika!

01:18:20.529 --> 01:18:22.323
Miyafuii!

01:18:22.531 --> 01:18:24.033
These voices!

01:18:29.205 --> 01:18:30.706
Ms. Miyafuji! Respond!

01:18:30.915 --> 01:18:33.250
Say something, Miyafuji!

01:18:33.459 --> 01:18:36.128
Are You okay, Miyafuji?!

01:18:36.337 --> 01:18:38.672
L-I can hear you...

01:18:38.881 --> 01:18:41.091
Are you all right, Ms. Miyafuji?!

01:18:41.300 --> 01:18:43.177
Yoshika! Say something!

01:18:43.385 --> 01:18:44.929
Hang on, Miyafuii!

01:18:45.137 --> 01:18:47.473
We're coming, Yoshika!

01:18:47.681 --> 01:18:50.517
Can you hear them, Ensign Miyafuji?

01:18:50.726 --> 01:18:52.478
Help is on the way!

01:18:54.688 --> 01:18:56.357
Miyafuji! Where are you?!

01:18:56.565 --> 01:18:58.567
Hang on, Yoshika!

01:19:00.152 --> 01:19:03.239
Everyone in the 501 st...

01:19:03.447 --> 01:19:05.699
...is calling for me...

01:19:07.159 --> 01:19:10.621
I... need to go...

01:19:16.001 --> 01:19:18.587
I-I'm done for...

01:19:19.713 --> 01:19:21.215
I need to go...

01:19:22.258 --> 01:19:26.887
I need to get to the others...!

01:19:27.096 --> 01:19:28.889
I need to go!

01:19:39.149 --> 01:19:41.235
Th-This light...!

01:19:56.542 --> 01:19:58.752
That light is from a magic circle!

01:19:58.961 --> 01:20:00.713
--Yoshika!
--It can't be!

01:20:00.921 --> 01:20:02.631
No way! That's impossible!

01:20:02.840 --> 01:20:05.676
I wouldn't be so sure, knowing Miyafuji.

01:20:05.884 --> 01:20:07.386
Shirley! Look!

01:20:07.594 --> 01:20:10.973
It's Miyafuji! She actually did it!

01:20:14.310 --> 01:20:17.771
My magic is back!

01:20:17.980 --> 01:20:20.441
E-Ensign Miyafuji!

01:20:27.990 --> 01:20:29.992
No way...

01:20:30.200 --> 01:20:31.994
But I already dealt with them!

01:20:37.708 --> 01:20:39.084
Artillery fire?!

01:20:39.293 --> 01:20:40.711
From where?!

01:20:47.134 --> 01:20:49.136
--Is that...
--...a battleship?!

01:20:49.345 --> 01:20:50.637
It's the Yamato!

01:20:50.846 --> 01:20:52.473
And it's in the Rhine!

01:20:52.681 --> 01:20:56.935
--It has inflatable tubes on it!
--The Fuso Navy is insane!

01:20:59.104 --> 01:21:01.607
My pupil's in trouble! Of course I'll act mad!

01:21:01.815 --> 01:21:03.484
That voice!

01:21:05.778 --> 01:21:07.946
"Fuso Imperial Navy Major
Sakamoto Mio" Major Sakamoto!

01:21:07.946 --> 01:21:08.238
Major Sakamoto!

01:21:08.447 --> 01:21:09.281
Mi¢>g

01:21:09.490 --> 01:21:12.201
It was the only way to keep her
off the river bottom!

01:21:12.409 --> 01:21:14.495
That's not exactly the crazy part...

01:21:14.703 --> 01:21:17.164
Hey. We're here, too.

01:21:17.373 --> 01:21:19.792
Ms. Eila! Sanya!

01:21:22.503 --> 01:21:25.422
Whoa! There's a whole swarm of 'em!

01:21:27.758 --> 01:21:28.801
Yahoo!

01:21:29.009 --> 01:21:30.636
We're here!

01:21:30.844 --> 01:21:32.763
Shirley! Lucchini!

01:21:32.971 --> 01:21:34.306
The whole gang's here.

01:21:34.515 --> 01:21:35.682
Mina!

01:21:35.891 --> 01:21:37.684
I brought Miyafuji a little souvenir!

01:21:37.893 --> 01:21:39.395
Cover me!

01:21:39.603 --> 01:21:40.854
Understood!

01:21:41.063 --> 01:21:43.232
Battle formation, everyone!

01:21:43.440 --> 01:21:45.984
Target all Neurois above the river!

01:21:46.193 --> 01:21:47.861
Let's give Major Sakamoto some cover!

01:21:48.070 --> 01:21:49.863
R°gefl

01:21:50.072 --> 01:21:51.865
N-No way...

01:21:52.074 --> 01:21:53.742
Are they seriously...?!

01:21:55.869 --> 01:21:57.413
Sturm!

01:21:59.540 --> 01:22:01.041
Tonnerre!

01:22:05.379 --> 01:22:07.339
Let's do it, Lucchini!

01:22:07.548 --> 01:22:08.674
Okay!

01:22:08.882 --> 01:22:10.008
Com-bine!

01:22:10.217 --> 01:22:14.179
Wh-Wh-Wha...?!

01:22:39.329 --> 01:22:41.665
W-Wow...

01:22:44.209 --> 01:22:45.711
Everyone!

01:22:46.962 --> 01:22:48.964
Here come some more!

01:22:49.173 --> 01:22:51.175
It's loaded for bear, that's for sure!

01:22:55.888 --> 01:22:57.931
I won't let you interfere!

01:23:03.061 --> 01:23:05.647
<i>Go'.!</i>

01:23:23.999 --> 01:23:26.668
Miyafuii!

01:23:26.877 --> 01:23:27.961
Major Sakamoto!

01:23:28.170 --> 01:23:30.297
This is for you!

01:23:42.684 --> 01:23:44.228
The Shinden?!

01:23:58.367 --> 01:24:00.285
Shinden...

01:24:00.494 --> 01:24:02.996
I want to go back.

01:24:03.205 --> 01:24:05.874
I want to be by their side again.

01:24:06.083 --> 01:24:08.085
So, please...

01:24:08.293 --> 01:24:09.795
Just once more...

01:24:10.796 --> 01:24:12.381
...let me fly!

01:24:25.185 --> 01:24:26.687
Take off!

01:24:36.363 --> 01:24:38.865
Yoshika!

01:24:39.074 --> 01:24:41.660
Lyme!

01:24:43.787 --> 01:24:45.539
Make it in time!

01:24:55.424 --> 01:24:57.426
Welcome back, Yoshika!

01:24:57.634 --> 01:24:59.344
It's good to be back, Lynne!

01:24:59.553 --> 01:25:04.349
Honestly, now. She never
ceases to be reckless.

01:25:04.558 --> 01:25:06.268
Yoshika's flying!

01:25:06.476 --> 01:25:08.437
Cool!

01:25:08.645 --> 01:25:11.356
How are you flying, Yoshika?!

01:25:11.565 --> 01:25:14.693
Especially after you lost your magic before!

01:25:14.901 --> 01:25:16.194
I'm not sure.

01:25:16.403 --> 01:25:21.825
But I heard all of your voices,
and my heart grew warm...

01:25:22.034 --> 01:25:24.536
And then I felt the need to help, too.

01:25:24.745 --> 01:25:26.788
Heh. Miyafuji.

01:25:26.997 --> 01:25:31.001
You want to help protect too, right?

01:25:33.920 --> 01:25:35.464
Yes!

01:25:35.672 --> 01:25:38.216
Oh, right! Shizuka!

01:25:38.425 --> 01:25:41.136
She's okay, Yoshika!

01:25:41.345 --> 01:25:43.096
UP here!

01:25:49.227 --> 01:25:51.063
Ensign Miyafuji...

01:25:52.773 --> 01:25:53.940
Shizuka...

01:25:54.149 --> 01:25:55.651
What a relief!

01:25:57.277 --> 01:25:58.737
Just as I always thought!

01:25:58.945 --> 01:26:02.866
The sky suits you the best, Miyafuji!

01:26:03.075 --> 01:26:05.535
It's where you belong!

01:26:05.744 --> 01:26:07.454
Ms. Sakamoto...

01:26:11.041 --> 01:26:12.542
Lieutenant Colonel Mina!

01:26:12.751 --> 01:26:16.463
We've been waiting for you,
Ms. Miyafuji. Can you fight?

01:26:16.672 --> 01:26:18.173
Yes!

01:26:34.606 --> 01:26:36.525
Whoa! It's huge!

01:26:36.733 --> 01:26:38.985
That's the enemy's main unit?!

01:26:39.194 --> 01:26:41.405
All members, Formation Julius!

01:26:41.613 --> 01:26:44.408
Our target is the colossal
Neuroi directly ahead!

01:26:44.616 --> 01:26:46.118
R°gefl

01:27:29.578 --> 01:27:32.581
So that's the legendary 501st?

01:27:32.789 --> 01:27:35.625
Yes. Those are the Strike Witches.

01:27:35.834 --> 01:27:40.630
Umm, how is Ensign Miyafuji able to fly again?

01:27:40.839 --> 01:27:43.383
That wasn't her power alone.

01:27:43.592 --> 01:27:47.971
The voices of her friends
in the 501 st helped her to fly.

01:27:48.180 --> 01:27:49.681
Friends?

01:27:52.017 --> 01:27:53.810
Will I...

01:27:54.019 --> 01:27:58.398
Will I ever be able to fly like that too?

01:28:01.818 --> 01:28:03.403
Of course you will!

01:28:14.372 --> 01:28:15.415
There's the core!

01:28:15.624 --> 01:28:18.043
Concentrate your fire on it, everyone!

01:28:24.716 --> 01:28:26.218
What now, Mina?!

01:28:27.636 --> 01:28:29.429
Yoshika!

01:28:29.638 --> 01:28:30.514
Miyafuii!

01:28:30.722 --> 01:28:32.307
"M going in!

01:28:33.934 --> 01:28:35.936
All members, deploy shields!

01:28:36.144 --> 01:28:37.604
Follow Ensign Miyafuji!

01:28:37.813 --> 01:28:39.314
R°gefl

01:28:45.529 --> 01:28:46.488
Are they serious?!

01:28:46.696 --> 01:28:48.406
Watch closely.

01:28:48.615 --> 01:28:50.534
They're what you should strive for.

01:28:50.742 --> 01:28:52.285
They're true Witches!

01:28:52.494 --> 01:28:55.038
<i>Go'.!</i>

01:29:35.912 --> 01:29:37.539
Ensign!

01:29:37.747 --> 01:29:40.000
Ensign Miyafuji!

01:29:40.208 --> 01:29:41.710
Shizuka!

01:29:44.963 --> 01:29:47.591
Shizuka! You don't need to call me "Ensign."

01:29:47.799 --> 01:29:49.301
Okay?

01:29:51.678 --> 01:29:54.097
Okay, Ms. Miyafuji!

01:30:05.525 --> 01:30:06.818
Lieutenant Colonel Mina.

01:30:07.027 --> 01:30:12.991
I've just received word that there are signs
of new Neurois near the Karlsland border.

01:30:14.409 --> 01:30:16.745
You heard her, everyone.

01:30:16.953 --> 01:30:22.334
There is only one option for us
to take against this new threat.

01:30:22.542 --> 01:30:27.505
The 501 st Joint Fighter Wing,
the Strike Witches,

01:30:27.714 --> 01:30:29.341
is hereby re-formed!

01:30:29.549 --> 01:30:31.051
R°gefl

01:30:53.740 --> 01:30:58.703
<i>As I take in a deep breath
while the sunlight caresses my hair,</i>

01:30:58.912 --> 01:31:03.792
<i>forgotten feelings race through my body</i>

01:31:04.000 --> 01:31:08.922
<i>I see you waiting excitedly with open arms</i>

01:31:09.130 --> 01:31:13.551
<i>"Come here! I'm here!"
you say as you beckon me</i>

01:31:13.760 --> 01:31:18.682
<i>into the endless sky
where our dreamt-of feelings</i>

01:31:18.890 --> 01:31:22.936
<i>are revealed with honesty</i>

01:31:23.144 --> 01:31:28.692
<i>The wind pushes me to the place
I want to return to</i>

01:31:28.900 --> 01:31:33.613
<i>as the wings on my back flutter</i>

01:31:33.822 --> 01:31:38.910
<i>There's a place I want to protect,
so I hold my hands up high</i>

01:31:39.119 --> 01:31:47.877
<i>with faith in what tomorrow will bring</i>

01:31:49.963 --> 01:31:54.801
<i>As I drive away my dreariness
amid the twinkling stars</i>

01:31:55.010 --> 01:31:59.973
<i>my body wells up with feelings I had long lost</i>

01:32:00.181 --> 01:32:05.061
<i>But I know I can reach you
without hesitation now</i>

01:32:05.270 --> 01:32:09.733
<i>so I say "I'm home" as loud as I can</i>

01:32:09.941 --> 01:32:14.821
<i>With tiny hands, we made a promise</i>

01:32:15.030 --> 01:32:19.117
<i>to set out into the sky</i>

01:32:19.325 --> 01:32:24.831
<i>As I wish for my dream to come true,
the wind touches my heart</i>

01:32:25.040 --> 01:32:29.753
<i>and fills my hands with strength</i>

01:32:29.961 --> 01:32:35.050
<i>To protect my dream, I wished so very hard</i>

01:32:35.258 --> 01:32:43.808
<i>for a bright, wonderful future</i>

01:33:03.203 --> 01:33:13.171
<i>Even if the looming darkness
is unavoidable fate</i>

01:33:13.379 --> 01:33:17.467
<i>I'll stand up to it! I refuse to give in!</i>

01:33:17.675 --> 01:33:24.224
<i>I'll use the magic only I can use</i>

01:33:24.432 --> 01:33:29.938
<i>A tailwind guides me
to the place I can return to</i>

01:33:30.146 --> 01:33:34.901
<i>and serves as my wings
in these wide, open skies</i>

01:33:35.110 --> 01:33:40.156
<i>And, once more,
because we have a place to protect</i>

01:33:40.365 --> 01:33:44.619
<i>we head into our own open skies</i>

01:33:44.828 --> 01:33:50.375
<i>The wind pushes me to the place
I want to return to</i>

01:33:50.583 --> 01:33:55.296
<i>as the wings on my back flutter</i>

01:33:55.505 --> 01:34:00.593
<i>There's a place I want to protect,
so I hold my hands up high</i>

01:34:00.802 --> 01:34:09.435
<i>with faith in what tomorrow will bring</i>

01:34:45.513 --> 01:34:49.726
"To Be Continued"
